{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1331105-sting-mage-what-not-to-do","id":1331105,"title":"STing Mage: What Not to do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-15T13:16:14-07:00","id":1331105,"title":"STing Mage: What Not to do?","content":"I was inspired to pose this question by a quality thread over in the Demon board, and being in the pondering stage of putting together ideas for a game of my own it felt like a good time to gather some ideas from the sagacious minds gathered here!<br /> <br /> So, what are some of the unique pitfalls to running mage? How does one best avoid them? Are their any glaring missteps yourself or your ST has made that you recommend I avoid (keeping this polite obviously).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T13:51:37-07:00","id":1331108,"title":"","content":"You want all the players on the same page. I know that sounds obvious, but it's a thing people often skip past. Make sure they understand the themes you're aiming for; a good way of doing this is to work with them to figure out how their cabal came together and what their mutual interests in being that cabal are (a specific mystery political goal, etc.). This is, from experience, the single most important things to do for the health of a game.<br /> <br /> From a mechanics standpoint: unless something significant is happening in it, if an Acanthus or someone with Time magic chooses to wind back the block you don't need to replay scenes, just bulletpoint how things would end up differently based on their choices. Similarly, you might feel inclined to kneejerk when reading Fate magic, but in practice the issues you might imagine come up about as often as any other potential abuse of power you can read from the other Arcana (which is rarely).<br /> <br /> Be willing to bend the rules a bit if someone is doing something sufficiently &quot;magical.&quot; If someone wants to Soul Jar a soul from one container to the other let them, there's no point in tearing your hair out in trying to determine if they need a higher Death or something in order to first sever it from the box it's currently in and no real verisimilitude in attempting to get that mechanistic--the exception to this is if you see a good story coming out of, though.<br /> <br /> Be prepared for any carefully-laid plans you have to likely come off the tracks at the earliest possible opportunity. Clever Mage players can accomplish most anything. The key is to be good at improvising, and focusing just as much on the <i>consequences</i> of their actions, intended and otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:23:56-07:00","id":1331114,"title":"","content":"I think it's only natural that your players will become interested in maybe minor elements you introduce in your games, They might be even become Obsessed. Don't make a fuss if they want to change their Obsessions to reflect it, even encourage it, The Obsession mechanic is after all, about what the player wants to see and explore in the game, and it's better if it rewards the players for doing the things they organically gravitates towards, instead of feeling either like a distraction or an obligation they are procrastinating.<br /> <br /> I mention this because just today I had a chat with a player I was seeing falling down a rabbit hole after interacting with a minor Mystery, and I think that's awesome, but he wasn't really advancing his original Obsession, so I asked him if he didn't want to change, at least until he becomes bored with his new Obsession and decides to go back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:26:53-07:00","id":1331115,"title":"","content":"Some general tips:<br /> <br /> 1- Don't rely on keeping details hidden, mages are the best equipped splat to figure out information. <br /> <br /> 2-Don't ask &quot;Can a player do this ?&quot; Because the answer is most likely yes. Magic is so flexible that a clever player can accomplish most things. Rather ask yourself what the consequences are for doing something or with a specific method.<br /> <br /> 3- Don't forget to talk to players on what kind of experience they want and discuss the feel the characters have. Their Awakenings are a great opportunity to foreshadow events, the Mystery Play can be useful to introduce Mysteries and Shadow Names can be a very useful foundation to build the story upon, acting as inspiration about their greater roll in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-15-2019, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T15:29:38-07:00","id":1331127,"title":"","content":"I cannot recommend <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> 's #3 more. Its soo soo soo good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T21:18:29-07:00","id":1332063,"title":"","content":"don't make antagonistic elements too narrow. A singular physical threat can be dealt with trivially. Organizations, groups, and situational problems are much harder to dump in an ocean.<br /> <br /> Similarly don't be afraid to make things complex with multiple plotlines colliding to make a mess.<br /> <br /> Finally, tell players what their charcters percieve, not what is there<br /> <br /> Don't forget other mages each have their own drives and unique flavors of bullshit reality warping","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}